Select panels whose daily statistics must be REPLACED, not increased. Nonselected valid panel totals are retained. Remaining aggregate energy is distributed by nominal power, keeping already recovered panel energy as a minimum. This is an estimated quarter-hour profile, not original panel measurements. Incomplete queued recoveries must finish compiling first.

repair_confirm.description:
**Date:** {date}  
**Aggregate production:** {aggregate} Wh  
**Statistical rows to change:** {rows}

| Panel | Current day (Wh) | Falling sums | Proposed day (Wh) |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
{panels}

The selected day is rebuilt using the aggregate profile. Later normalized sums are shifted to preserve subsequent energy increments and align hourly/five-minute statistics. Live sensor totals, original state history and recovery amounts stay unchanged. Other dates with independent negative increments need their own repair.

Previous values are saved before the database transaction. Only the latest repair can be undone; applying a new repair replaces the previous checkpoint. Undo is refused if other corrections changed saved rows.
